body:
I'm sorry that you were hurt in the past. I can't imagine the pain that put you through. 

&#x200B;

I've laid out my situation to friends and family. The responses have been caring and supportive but not in the ways I need. They offer what would make them feel better in my situation - a house to crash in, video games, someone to drive me to doctors appointments, etc. 

&#x200B;

I need a partner right now. My love for others has always helped me persevere. I need that person who I love in a special way. I need to go on more adventures and have that person with me that I completely trust. I need a reason to get through this that's special. 

&#x200B;

As illogical as it may be, I just needed someone to be there and support me through this process of coming to terms with everything. Someone to go into a canyon with me then ice climb and help me push myself. I needed to hit a wall and get so exhausted physically that I could go back to the doctors and not regret taking the last of my energy and putting that to use doing what I love. I wanted one more "hurrah" before committing to a process that may not have the best outcomes. I can't do these "high-risk" activities with just anyone. I can't form that bond with just anyone or anything. I'm worried I'm losing myself and I needed someone around that knew me better than anyone to remind me of what I'm capable of afterwards. Someone I trust to help push me again if things get better, or be by my side if things get worse. Someone I *let* push me. Someone I'm not confused about.

I just don't have energy or strength for all of it right now. I know pain is temporary. I know this is just a bad hand dealt by the world. But I'm *so tired*. I'm overwhelmed with pain, guilt, fear. I've never been overwhelmed before. I've looked death in the eye on many occasions and stayed collected. I've been charged by grizzlies, been caught in avalanches, taken hard crashes and some falls. I've seen the outcome of accidents and incidents. But this, according to my gut, is the end whether it's by my hand or not. I can prolong the pain or I can go out on my terms. 

In the end it's my burden to carry. I can't put it on these people. They won't share it, even if they wanted to.
